  "seoBody": "<p>Quickler runs inspection and compliance workflows over WhatsApp. Because the field worker only needs the WhatsApp account already on their phone, quickler works the same way in London, Lyon or Los Angeles. There is no national app store to clear, no local hardware to ship, and no country-specific install. The product has deep roots in UK compliance and is used by firms in the UK, Europe and the United States.</p><h2>WhatsApp, photos and a web report need no local infrastructure.</h2><p>Most field software is tied to a place by its plumbing: an app store listing per region, SMS gateways per country, hardware to distribute. Quickler avoids all of that by running on infrastructure that is already global.</p><ul><li>WhatsApp is installed on over two billion phones across almost every country</li><li>Field workers use the account they already have, with nothing new to download</li><li>Photos and voice notes work identically on any network</li><li>The output is a shareable web report and a permanent record, with optional PDF export, which mean the same thing everywhere</li><li>Data is held on EU servers, a neutral and privacy-respecting base for any region</li></ul><p>The result is a field compliance tool that a firm in the United States or mainland Europe can adopt in exactly the same week, and the same way, as a firm in the UK.</p><h2>UK certificates were the starting point, not the ceiling.</h2><p>Quickler was first built around UK compliance work, EICR electrical reports, CP12 gas safety certificates, van walkround checks, because that is where it started. But the engine underneath is form-agnostic.</p><ul><li>Upload your own inspection or safety form, in any country</li><li>Quickler turns it into a guided WhatsApp workflow automatically</li><li>US site safety walks, fleet and equipment checks, European field records all run the same way</li><li>Condition ratings, defect logging, photos and sign-off carry across borders unchanged</li></ul><p>If your team inspects something and writes it down, quickler can run it, wherever in the world the inspection happens.</p><h2>Built by people who have shipped field and data software internationally.</h2><h3>Where Quickler is rooted</h3><p>Quickler's first customers are UK trades and inspection firms running EICR, gas, van and site safety workflows. The UK is where the product was proven against real regulatory work.</p><h3>International delivery in the team's DNA</h3><p>Quickler's founder has previously built and delivered field and data software for US customers in a prior venture. That international experience is why the product was designed to be country-agnostic from day one.</p><h3>An EU-hosted base</h3><p>With data hosted in Germany and a GDPR-aligned design, quickler is a natural fit for field compliance work across the European Union.</p><h2>Using Quickler outside the UK.</h2><h3>Does it work in the US?</h3><p>Yes. WhatsApp is widely used in the US and quickler runs over it exactly as it does in the UK. Upload your inspection or safety form and quickler builds the workflow.</p><h3>Does it work in Europe?</h3><p>Yes. Data is hosted in the EU and the product is GDPR-aligned, which suits firms across the European Union.</p><h3>Do I have to use UK certificate types?</h3><p>No. EICR and CP12 are just examples. You can upload any form from any country and run it as a WhatsApp workflow.</p><h3>What currency is pricing in?</h3><p>Pricing is quoted in GBP, with EUR and USD available on request. You add your whole team and only pay for who actually works, since dormant users are free.</p><h3>What language are workflows in?</h3><p>Workflows run in English today, with further languages on the roadmap.</p><h3>How do I get started?</h3><p>Start free at <a href=\"https://app.quickler.co/signup\">app.quickler.co/signup</a>, with no card and no trial clock, or <a href=\"/pages/help/index.html#contact-form-section\">get in touch</a> to talk through a workflow for your country.</p>",
